<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Doti</h1><p class="st-meta">1400 CE – 1790 CE (approx.) · capital Dipayal</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A hill kingdom of far-western Nepal ruled by the Raika kings, one of the successor states of the Khasa Malla realm.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Doti emerged from the break-up of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/khasa-malla-kingdom">Khasa Malla kingdom</a> in the late 14th century, in the hills between the Karnali and Mahakali rivers. Its rulers, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raika-dynasty">Raika dynasty</a>, are traditionally said to descend from the Katyuri kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumaon">Kumaon</a> and established themselves at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dipayal-silgadhi">Dipayal</a> and nearby seats.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Doti was one of the larger of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baise-rajya">Baise Rajya</a>, the twenty-two hill kingdoms of the Karnali region. Its kings ruled through local chiefs and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> advisers, and fought their neighbours the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kumaon-kingdom">Kumaon Kingdom</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-jumla">Kingdom of Jumla</a>. Inscriptions and temple grants are the main sources, and the Doteli dialect of Nepali takes its name from the kingdom.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The expanding <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gorkha-kingdom">Gorkha</a> armies of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Kingdom of Nepal</a> conquered Doti around 1790, defeating its last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raika-dynasty">Raika</a> king. Doti became a district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, and the name survives in Doti district and the Doteli language.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1400 CE – 1790 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H